  "question": {
    "text": "If arithmetic mean of two distinct positive real number $a$ and $b(a \\gt b)$ be twice their geometric mean, then $a: b=$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "k15lS",
      "text": "$(2+\\sqrt{3}):(2-\\sqrt{3})$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "4gLF5",
      "text": "$(2+\\sqrt{5}):(2-\\sqrt{5})$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "k1nwn",
      "text": "$(2+\\sqrt{2}):(2-\\sqrt{2})$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PBmTe",
      "text": "None of these",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "By the given condition,\n$\\frac{a+b}{2}=2 \\sqrt{a b} \\Rightarrow a+b=4 \\sqrt{a b}$\nNow, $(a-b)^2=(a+b)^2-4 a b=16 a b-4 a b=$ $12 a b$\n$\\therefore a-b=\\sqrt{12 a b}=2 \\sqrt{3} \\sqrt{a b}$.\n(Taking + ve sign only as $a \\gt b$)\n$\\therefore \\frac{a+b}{a-b}=\\frac{4 \\sqrt{a b}}{2 \\sqrt{3} \\sqrt{a b}}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$\nBy componendo and dividendo,\n$\\frac{2 a}{2 b}=\\frac{2+\\sqrt{3}}{2-\\sqrt{3}}$ or $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{2+\\sqrt{3}}{2-\\sqrt{3}}$",
    "image": null
  },
